WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:03.690
- [Mark] Alright, Marty.

00:00:03.690 --> 00:00:04.610
Marty, where'd you grow up?

00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:06.660
Where are you from originally?

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:08.010
- [Marty] I'm from Vallejo.

00:00:09.010 --> 00:00:09.880
- [Mark] And tell me about your childhood.

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:12.120
You had both your parents
when you were a kid?

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:13.270
- [Marty] No, I didn't.

00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:16.580
- [Mark] Who raised you?

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:24.443
- My dad, I guess.

00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:30.410
- [Mark] Where was your mom?

00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:31.290
- My mom was...

00:00:32.912 --> 00:00:33.745
I was found

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:38.620
as a little child

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:40.653
with the famous note.

00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:44.143
So I don't know.

00:00:44.143 --> 00:00:48.520
I never met my real blood parents before.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:49.980
- [Mark] So the father that raised you

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:51.740
was just somebody who kind of adopted you?

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:52.573
- Yes.

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:55.190
- [Mark] How was your childhood?

00:00:55.190 --> 00:00:57.253
- It was pretty foul.

00:00:58.200 --> 00:00:59.757
I was more or less

00:01:01.307 --> 00:01:04.623
locked up in a room with no lock on it.

00:01:08.737 --> 00:01:11.567
- [Mark] For how long?

00:01:11.567 --> 00:01:13.963
- Since before I was 16.

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:20.340
- [Mark] Look I mean there was child abuse

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:21.280
and stuff like that going on?

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:22.260
- Yes.

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:24.520
- [Mark] What kind of stuff was going on?

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:29.520
- Just not get anything to eat for...

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:40.883
- [Mark] How long would
you go without eating?

00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:44.400
- Almost every day.

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:45.910
I wouldn't eat until my

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:50.803
dad would come home from work.

00:01:51.810 --> 00:01:54.150
And I'd finally get to come

00:01:54.150 --> 00:01:56.053
outside my room and get some dinner.

00:01:56.990 --> 00:02:00.430
- [Mark] So your adopted
family was good to you,

00:02:00.430 --> 00:02:02.050
or they were mean to you?

00:02:02.050 --> 00:02:03.530
- Yeah, they were...

00:02:05.523 --> 00:02:07.653
My dad tried.

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:09.473
He tried.

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:12.270
He tried for a long time,

00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:13.620
but they fought every night

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:17.193
over me or money.

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:20.850
- [Mark] Were you the only child?

00:02:20.850 --> 00:02:22.663
- Yes, no I wasn't.

00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:25.590
I had two

00:02:27.050 --> 00:02:30.683
here on earth brothers.

00:02:34.860 --> 00:02:37.063
- [Mark] What kind of kid
were you in high school?

00:02:37.063 --> 00:02:39.423
- I was a pretty good kid in high school,

00:02:40.330 --> 00:02:43.390
especially after I left home.

00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:44.450
I went to stay

00:02:44.450 --> 00:02:46.350
with my aunt Gladys and my aunt Gladys

00:02:47.660 --> 00:02:49.860
she took me shopping for the first time.

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:51.470
I got some real nice school clothes

00:02:51.470 --> 00:02:52.770
and I got me a girlfriend.

00:02:58.230 --> 00:02:59.563
Real fast, like.

00:03:02.042 --> 00:03:04.563
A girl named Janet.

00:03:08.360 --> 00:03:11.793
Janet Fisher.

00:03:13.470 --> 00:03:16.820
- [Mark] So your aunt Gladys
was a blood relative of yours?

00:03:16.820 --> 00:03:18.900
- No, she wasn't blood, but she was

00:03:21.354 --> 00:03:22.304
a relative of mine.

00:03:24.150 --> 00:03:25.270
- [Mark] So she was like some relation

00:03:25.270 --> 00:03:26.103
to your adopted parents?

00:03:26.103 --> 00:03:26.960
- Yes, yes.

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:28.175
- [Mark] Okay.

00:03:28.175 --> 00:03:30.670
- She was my...

00:03:31.909 --> 00:03:33.326
Him and our dad's

00:03:35.603 --> 00:03:38.543
brother-in-law brother. (mumbles)

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:42.243
- [Mark] And you went out
on your own at what age?

00:03:43.720 --> 00:03:47.533
- I was on my own since
I was probably 15, 16.

00:03:48.874 --> 00:03:50.874
- [Mark] And where'd you go at that age?

00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:54.137
- I went to stay with

00:03:57.120 --> 00:04:01.980
some relatives of mine until...

00:04:06.940 --> 00:04:09.280
You know I ended up stealing some money

00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:11.400
from one of my relatives.

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:14.720
'Cause my aunt got in a big
argument with my parents.

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:16.970
My parents weren't sending them any money

00:04:16.970 --> 00:04:18.860
and I didn't realize how
much food I was eatin'

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:20.830
out of the house.

00:04:20.830 --> 00:04:23.220
And my aunt she told me

00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:24.053
she can't deal with it.

00:04:24.053 --> 00:04:26.500
And she told me to get the fuck out

00:04:28.063 --> 00:04:29.410
of her house.

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:30.350
And I did.

00:04:30.350 --> 00:04:35.080
But I remember finding some
money inside her dresser

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:36.254
that my cousin told me

00:04:36.254 --> 00:04:40.810
to go get her a wrap
for her boyfriend Mark.

00:04:40.810 --> 00:04:43.403
And that next to the wrap
was a big wad of money.

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:46.030
And so I remember that wad of money.

00:04:46.030 --> 00:04:49.050
So I remember when my aunt
told me to get the fuck out.

00:04:49.050 --> 00:04:51.467
I said, "Well, I'm not
going to leave empty handed.

00:04:51.467 --> 00:04:53.117
"I'm only 16 years old.

00:04:53.117 --> 00:04:55.120
"I got nowhere to go at 16."

00:04:55.120 --> 00:04:56.020
So I took the money

00:04:56.020 --> 00:04:57.270
and I went all the way to

00:05:05.814 --> 00:05:06.981
West Virginia.

00:05:12.708 --> 00:05:14.291
When I was only 16.

00:05:15.950 --> 00:05:17.443
- [Mark] Do you have kids of your own?

00:05:18.350 --> 00:05:19.450
- Yes, I do.

00:05:19.450 --> 00:05:20.980
- [Mark] And where are they?

00:05:20.980 --> 00:05:22.080
- I've got a son who's

00:05:25.002 --> 00:05:26.903
a Harvard Law School graduate.

00:05:27.820 --> 00:05:28.653
Believe it or not.

00:05:28.653 --> 00:05:31.517
His name is Christian Phillip Gillis.

00:05:31.517 --> 00:05:33.510
I have his tattoo on my chest,

00:05:33.510 --> 00:05:34.720
Christian Phillip.

00:05:34.720 --> 00:05:35.780
- [Mark] This is your son?

00:05:35.780 --> 00:05:36.613
- Yes.

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:38.393
- [Mark] Do you stay in contact

00:05:38.393 --> 00:05:39.750
with your family or your son?

00:05:40.830 --> 00:05:41.663
- I've tried to.

00:05:46.300 --> 00:05:48.693
- [Mark] So today you're
living in the Tenderloin?

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:52.110
- Yes I'm out there in the chill

00:05:52.110 --> 00:05:54.320
and I'm out there on the streets

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:55.670
of San Francisco right now.

00:05:57.319 --> 00:05:59.423
- [Mark] And how long have
you been living in Tenderloin?

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:02.273
- For about

00:06:05.713 --> 00:06:07.163
three and a half years or so.

00:06:08.140 --> 00:06:09.161
- [Mark] And you're living

00:06:09.161 --> 00:06:11.320
in a tent or just on the street?

00:06:11.320 --> 00:06:13.153
- I'm livin' out there

00:06:17.944 --> 00:06:19.763
on the streets.

00:06:21.188 --> 00:06:22.240
- [Mark] No tent.

00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:23.073
- No tent.

00:06:24.503 --> 00:06:26.393
- [Mark] And what do you do for money now?

00:06:26.393 --> 00:06:27.510
How do you survive?

00:06:27.510 --> 00:06:28.563
- I was getting SSI

00:06:31.693 --> 00:06:34.776
and I haven't been able to find my...

00:06:37.840 --> 00:06:41.560
I have what they call

00:06:45.454 --> 00:06:49.650
payees through a place called Walden House

00:06:49.650 --> 00:06:53.980
and haven't been able to find them

00:06:55.840 --> 00:07:00.370
my two payees

00:07:00.370 --> 00:07:02.893
named Lynette and Annette.

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:06.048
They're my payees.

00:07:06.048 --> 00:07:07.689
- [Mark] Okay.

00:07:07.689 --> 00:07:10.830
- I have been eatin' out
of garbage cans since then.

00:07:14.440 --> 00:07:15.273
- [Mark] Do you use any

00:07:15.273 --> 00:07:16.520
of the drugs that are on the street?

00:07:17.824 --> 00:07:18.657
- I do.

00:07:20.521 --> 00:07:22.727
I do some crank out there.

00:07:23.820 --> 00:07:25.910
- [Mark] And crank is what?

00:07:25.910 --> 00:07:26.780
- It's meth.

00:07:26.780 --> 00:07:27.613
- [Mark] Crystal meth?

00:07:27.613 --> 00:07:28.661
- Yes.

00:07:28.661 --> 00:07:29.780
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:07:29.780 --> 00:07:31.619
How long have you been using crank?

00:07:31.619 --> 00:07:33.377
- I've been using off and on.

00:07:34.293 --> 00:07:36.530
I only need a shot every month or so.

00:07:36.530 --> 00:07:39.680
So a good shot will do me.

00:07:39.680 --> 00:07:41.670
I haven't had a good shot in probably

00:07:44.040 --> 00:07:45.213
three or four years.

00:07:47.347 --> 00:07:48.180
I can't remember that.

00:07:48.180 --> 00:07:49.277
I think I paid a guy $100

00:07:51.370 --> 00:07:52.763
to shoot me one time.

00:07:55.794 --> 00:07:57.570
To fix me.

00:07:57.570 --> 00:07:58.403
To...

00:08:10.902 --> 00:08:12.790
- [Mark] Do you drink
alcohol sometimes as well?

00:08:12.790 --> 00:08:13.623
- No.

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:16.070
I don't like alcohol too much.

00:08:16.070 --> 00:08:17.910
I drink every now and then

00:08:17.910 --> 00:08:19.663
to come down off of crack.

00:08:22.293 --> 00:08:25.270
- [Mark] Have you ever been
in a mental health facility

00:08:25.270 --> 00:08:27.313
or gotten counseling
or anything like that?

00:08:29.650 --> 00:08:30.483
- No.

00:08:38.020 --> 00:08:39.913
- [Mark] When did you
first start using drugs?

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:53.550
- About three or four...

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:59.800
Noe, about seven years
ago in 2012. (gulps)

00:09:07.080 --> 00:09:08.383
- [Mark] Do you have any friends?

00:09:09.600 --> 00:09:10.433
- I have some.

00:09:12.030 --> 00:09:14.930
More like associates.

00:09:14.930 --> 00:09:17.023
- [Mark] It's just people
you meet on the street?

00:09:18.440 --> 00:09:21.490
- I have some good friends
and family out there

00:09:21.490 --> 00:09:25.433
who don't use whatsoever.

00:09:31.730 --> 00:09:32.910
- [Mark] Do you think
anything in your childhood

00:09:32.910 --> 00:09:35.290
might have led you into this lifestyle

00:09:35.290 --> 00:09:37.893
of homelessness and drugs
and stuff like that?

00:09:40.420 --> 00:09:42.550
It sounds like your
childhood was kind of rough.

00:09:42.550 --> 00:09:44.650
- Yes, it has been.

00:09:51.730 --> 00:09:52.660
- [Mark] How do you think you've changed

00:09:52.660 --> 00:09:54.710
from all these years of living like this?

00:09:57.080 --> 00:09:58.180
- [Marty] I've changed for the better.

00:09:58.180 --> 00:10:00.033
I've changed.

00:10:05.760 --> 00:10:07.240
It's kind of hard to explain

00:10:07.240 --> 00:10:08.490
after all the...

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:17.500
I went through a whole lot for

00:10:19.400 --> 00:10:20.980
a lot of people's souls.

00:10:20.980 --> 00:10:21.813
I really did.

00:10:24.060 --> 00:10:27.050
I am whom it came down to.

00:10:27.050 --> 00:10:28.000
It came down to me.

00:10:31.564 --> 00:10:32.860
- [Mark] Have you had
bad things happen to you

00:10:32.860 --> 00:10:33.960
living in the streets?

00:10:37.440 --> 00:10:39.211
- No, no.

00:10:39.211 --> 00:10:40.044
No.

00:10:41.610 --> 00:10:43.040
- [Mark] People leave you alone?

00:10:43.040 --> 00:10:44.520
- Pretty much yes they do.

00:10:48.207 --> 00:10:49.550
- [Mark] What's the most important lesson

00:10:49.550 --> 00:10:51.700
you've learned in your life?

00:10:51.700 --> 00:10:53.240
How old are you?

00:10:53.240 --> 00:10:54.090
- I'm 53.

00:10:54.090 --> 00:10:54.923
- [Mark] 53.

00:10:57.870 --> 00:10:58.703
What do you think

00:10:58.703 --> 00:11:01.223
the most important thing
you've learned in your life?

00:11:14.460 --> 00:11:16.167
- Don't trust anyone (soft chuckle).

00:11:27.360 --> 00:11:29.360
- [Mark] Do you feel you
have anyone you can go to

00:11:29.360 --> 00:11:30.260
in a time of need?

00:11:44.452 --> 00:11:45.500
- No, I don't.

00:11:45.500 --> 00:11:46.333
I don't

00:11:50.170 --> 00:11:51.690
remember some of

00:11:53.125 --> 00:11:55.240
my own family's phone number.

00:11:55.240 --> 00:11:59.033
I don't know if my dad's
even livin' right now.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:01.700
I haven't called my dad in a while

00:12:02.840 --> 00:12:05.440
after that situation
happened when I was stuck

00:12:11.230 --> 00:12:14.573
in a elevator with this girl.

00:12:16.510 --> 00:12:19.370
- [Mark] What happened in
the elevator with the girl?

00:12:19.370 --> 00:12:20.670
- She wanted me to call my dad up

00:12:20.670 --> 00:12:22.070
and get some money from him.

00:12:26.240 --> 00:12:27.073
And I did.

00:12:27.073 --> 00:12:29.200
I lied to my dad about

00:12:30.948 --> 00:12:32.680
why I needed some money.

00:12:32.680 --> 00:12:34.730
And my dad ended up finding out about it.

00:12:45.800 --> 00:12:48.200
- [Mark] So Marty, how will
you spend the rest of the day?

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:50.780
It's a Saturday morning
here in San Francisco.

00:12:50.780 --> 00:12:53.340
What will you do the rest of the day?

00:12:53.340 --> 00:12:54.660
- I'll use the money

00:12:55.680 --> 00:12:57.913
that you're gonna give me.

00:13:00.683 --> 00:13:01.870
I'll probably go

00:13:02.820 --> 00:13:05.310
buy me some crystal

00:13:09.480 --> 00:13:11.010
and get high with it.

00:13:11.010 --> 00:13:13.423
'Cause it helps me stay warm at night.

00:13:15.280 --> 00:13:18.000
- [Mark] That's basically your
existence everyday down here?

00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:18.833
- Pretty much.

00:13:21.550 --> 00:13:22.680
- [Mark] Do you have hope

00:13:22.680 --> 00:13:24.730
of a different life for you for yourself?

00:13:25.860 --> 00:13:26.693
- Yes, I do.

00:13:26.693 --> 00:13:27.526
I'm hoping to get

00:13:29.670 --> 00:13:30.970
dropped off by my family

00:13:30.970 --> 00:13:35.160
and dropped off the street.

00:13:42.053 --> 00:13:43.600
- [Mark] But you haven't
spoken to your family

00:13:43.600 --> 00:13:44.433
in a long time.

00:13:45.350 --> 00:13:46.470
- No.

00:13:46.470 --> 00:13:48.540
- [Mark] You don't have their phone number

00:13:48.540 --> 00:13:50.430
and they don't know where
you are probably, right?

00:13:50.430 --> 00:13:51.263
- No.

00:14:00.820 --> 00:14:02.970
- [Mark] Have you been
in love before, Marty?

00:14:02.970 --> 00:14:04.730
- Have I been in love before?

00:14:04.730 --> 00:14:05.563
- [Mark] Yes.

00:14:05.563 --> 00:14:06.396
- Yes, I have.

00:14:10.233 --> 00:14:11.740
- [Mark] Were you married before?

00:14:11.740 --> 00:14:12.573
- No.

00:14:20.040 --> 00:14:21.733
- [Mark] What was the
best time of your life?

00:14:25.650 --> 00:14:26.960
- The best, the worst time?

00:14:26.960 --> 00:14:28.033
- [Mark] The best time.

00:14:38.190 --> 00:14:39.090
- When I first saw

00:14:44.366 --> 00:14:46.199
my future queen I fell

00:14:48.208 --> 00:14:50.020
in love with her as soon as I seen her.

00:14:50.020 --> 00:14:52.080
I said to myself, "Who is that?"

00:14:52.080 --> 00:14:54.297
I go, "She's walking with a purpose,

00:14:54.297 --> 00:14:55.737
"she's walking with a purpose.

00:14:55.737 --> 00:14:56.967
"One day I will marry her

00:14:56.967 --> 00:15:00.097
"and she'll never, never,
never, never, never, never

00:15:00.097 --> 00:15:02.620
"never, never, never,
never, never, never, never

00:15:03.797 --> 00:15:06.247
"never, never, never,
never, never, never, never,

00:15:15.521 --> 00:15:17.771
"She will never betray me."

00:15:26.390 --> 00:15:27.223
- [Mark] Alright, Marty.

00:15:27.223 --> 00:15:28.056
Thank you so much for talking with me

00:15:28.056 --> 00:15:31.100
and good luck with wherever
you go from here, man.

00:15:31.100 --> 00:15:31.940
- Thank you, Sir.

00:15:31.940 --> 00:15:33.373
- [Mark] I appreciate it your time.

00:15:34.360 --> 00:15:35.193
Thank you, man.

00:15:46.859 --> 00:15:47.692
Alright.

